led to massive throttling issues  and super annoying fans even when  browsing the web and doing simple zoom  calls  now the next disappointment involves m1  max  first the m1 macbook only natively  supports one external display  which hasn't been a limitation with max  for like almost 10 years  now and this alone caused people to go  for an intel macbook instead  or wait for a future apple silicon model  second the new m1 mac mini for some  reason  only has two thunderbolt ports or  previously  the intel mini came with four ports and  guess what the m1 mini actually supports  four ports let me explain owc dug deep  into figuring out the reason behind the  lack of the extra ports  and they discovered that apple is  actually using two separate thunderbolt  controllers just like the old mini which  has four ports  and m1 actually supports thunderbolt 4  but apple couldn't call them that  because they only support one display  apple could have technically given the  m1 for thunderbolt ports but they  decided to limit it and that's a huge  fail  because we can no longer get 10 gigabit  ethernet as well  meaning that max can't connect to our  server and those two ports are full from  his display and our qnap  moving on to the next one let's talk  about the iphone 12 pro max  when apple first announced the best  cameras only coming on the pro max  quite a few people including max bought  it just for that  but it turned out to be a bit of a  disappointment  the main camera is only slightly better  but the two and a half times  lens looks worse than the two times on  the pro more often than not  that's because the aperture went from f  2.0 to f 2.2 in order to achieve the two  and a half times  zoom and that means that it takes in  less light because of that  photos in lower light look worse with  more noise and more motion blur as well  portrait mode photos suffer even more  since they require more light  so in many cases max and vadim have been  using the main camera  way 