ry weak  so it constantly slips off when you're  putting it into your pocket for instance  and that's honestly pretty scary always  having to risk it falling off somewhere  losing your cards  the 12 mini is the only phone we can  recommend it for  because it fits perfectly and doesn't  slip off but  apple could have fixed this by using  stronger magnets the next fail of the  year is the iconic  thousand dollar stand for the mac pro  now the fail actually isn't the pricing  of the stain itself  since it's machined out of a solid block  of aluminum and you could easily adjust  the display  by just using one finger but it was the  way the apple announced it  just watch for yourself  hey guys it's max here it looks like  that was such  a fail for apple that angelica has tried  to upload this video  twice and modified that clip and apple  keeps blocking it from youtube and not  even allowing us  to post our video so basically what  happened here  is that apple showed off the xdr they  showed off  the stand and then when they gave the  price the whole crowd  kind of had this collective grunt of  disappointment  for a thousand dollar stand and that  does  once again prove our point probably even  more so  that this stand from apple was a massive  fail or at least the way they handled it  everyone was shocked by the pricing  which is understandable  but that wouldn't have happened if apple  just said the display is six thousand  dollars and if you don't want the stand  then you get a thousand dollars off the  last failure of the year is the mac  pro and not because it's a bad product  but just because of how fast it's aged  and not in the way most expected like  older pci slots or cpu sockets but  because of apple's own  m1 processors making the beast seem  outdated now sure  a mac mini won't replace the crazy  high-end configs or expandability of the  mac pro  but we've already seen many people say  that they're going to wait for an m1 mac  pro instead  and max himself is 